# Studio background isolation

**Official policy.** The studio viewport canvas backing is a separate layer from UI chrome (export overlay, dropzone, shelf scrims, html boot, etc.). When the user asks to change the **studio background**, touch studio tokens only — never `--orby-app-bg`, `--orby-black`, or `ORBY_BLACK` unless they explicitly ask for UI-wide black.

## Tokens

| Layer | CSS | JS |
|-------|-----|-----|
| **Studio viewport** | `--orby-studio-bg` | `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` (`scripts/constants.js`) |
| **UI chrome** | `--orby-app-bg` / `--orby-black` | `ORBY_BLACK` |
| **3D clear / backdrop panel** | — (runtime via `BackgroundController`) | `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` / `APP_BACKGROUND` |
| **21∶9 letterbox** | `--cinematic-letterbox-black` | `CINEMATIC_LETTERBOX_BLACK` |

Defined in `styles.css`:

```css
--orby-black: #080808;
--orby-app-bg: var(--orby-black);
--orby-studio-bg: var(--orby-black); /* JS overrides when backdrop applies; default = transition black */
```

## CSS selectors (studio only)

- `.viewport` → `var(--orby-studio-bg)`
- `#webgl` → `var(--orby-studio-bg)`

## CSS selectors (UI — do not retarget when changing studio bg)

- `.viewport-offline-export` (rendering overlay)
- `.dropzone`
- `html`, `body`, `.workspace` (shell pending)
- `.orby-sr` (screen-reader / boot shell)
- Frosted panels, modals, toasts → `--ui-frosted-bg`, `--orby-app-bg`, `--orby-black`

## Do

- User says “change studio bg” → update `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` and rely on `syncStudioBackgroundColor` for `--orby-studio-bg`
- Default `--orby-studio-bg` in CSS stays `var(--orby-black)` — transitions / load spinner never flash studio gray
- Scene backdrop color from the Background panel stays in JS state / `BackgroundController` — not `--orby-app-bg`

## Transitions (always Orby black)

Page transitions lock the viewport to `#080808` via `scripts/ui/orbyPageTransition.js`:

- `html.orby-page-transition` (load spinner + dropzone hide)
- CSS `:has(.dropzone.hiding)` / `:has(.viewport-load-spinner.is-visible)`
- WebGL clear color forced to `TRANSITION_BACKDROP` until unlock

After the spinner ends **and** the dropzone hide animation completes, `flushStudioViewportBackdrop()` applies `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` (`#252525`).

## Don't

- Change `--orby-app-bg` or `--orby-black` when the user only asked for studio background
- Point `.viewport-offline-export`, `.dropzone`, or overlay scrims at `--orby-studio-bg`
- Alias `--orby-studio-bg` to `--orby-app-bg` — that re-couples the layers

## Manual verify

1. Change `--orby-studio-bg` to a distinct color (e.g. `#1a1a2e`) — viewport letterboxing around WebGL updates; export overlay and dropzone stay `#080808`
2. Studio → Background color picker — 3D backdrop updates; rendering overlay unchanged
